 r←Test_Misc_024(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;md;removed;txt;CRLF
⍝ Exercise `RemoveHtmlTags`
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed
 CRLF←##.Server.CRLF

⍝ ------------- HTML tags are removed, and that is reported back
 (md removed)←##.Server.RemoveHtmlTags'Hi <b>there</b>!'
 →T.PassesIf'Hi there!'≡md
 →T.PassesIf 1=removed

 (md removed)←##.Server.RemoveHtmlTags'<img src="x" onerror="alert(1)">'
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢md
 →T.PassesIf 1=removed

⍝ ------------- Automatic links are not HTML tags: they must survive untouched
 txt←'See <https://tatin.dev>, <http://tatin.dev>, <ftp://foo.com> and <file://bar>'
 (md removed)←##.Server.RemoveHtmlTags txt
 →T.PassesIf txt≡md
 →T.PassesIf 0=removed

 txt←'Write to <mailto:kai@aplteam.com> or simply <kai@aplteam.com>'
 (md removed)←##.Server.RemoveHtmlTags txt
 →T.PassesIf txt≡md
 →T.PassesIf 0=removed

⍝ ------------- Neither is a tag in inline code: MarkAPL escapes those anyway
 txt←'Use `<b>bold</b>` in order to get bold'
 (md removed)←##.Server.RemoveHtmlTags txt
 →T.PassesIf txt≡md
 →T.PassesIf 0=removed

 (md removed)←##.Server.RemoveHtmlTags'Use `<b>` but not <i>this</i>'
 →T.PassesIf'Use `<b>` but not this'≡md
 →T.PassesIf 1=removed

⍝ ------------- ... nor a tag between a pair of fences
 txt←'text',CRLF,'```',CRLF,'<div>raw</div>',CRLF,'```'
 (md removed)←##.Server.RemoveHtmlTags txt
 →T.PassesIf txt≡md
 →T.PassesIf 0=removed

 txt←'a',CRLF,'   ~~~ apl',CRLF,'<span>x</span>',CRLF,'~~~'
 (md removed)←##.Server.RemoveHtmlTags txt
 →T.PassesIf txt≡md
 →T.PassesIf 0=removed

⍝ ------------- ... but a tag after the closing fence is still a tag
 txt←'```',CRLF,'<div>ok</div>',CRLF,'```',CRLF,'<em>no</em>'
 (md removed)←##.Server.RemoveHtmlTags txt
 →T.PassesIf 1=removed

⍝ ------------- Nothing at all is fine as well
 (md removed)←##.Server.RemoveHtmlTags''
 →T.PassesIf 0=≢md
 →T.PassesIf 0=removed

 r←T._OK
⍝Done
